      "message": "[error] Line 63: 🔴 The recursive callback captures and uses `handler` inside its own initializer (`std::function\u003cvoid()\u003e handler \u003d [\u0026] { ... handler(); };`). This pattern is compiler-sensitive and can fail or warn-as-error (notably on GCC/MSVC), which matches the failing Linux/MSVC jobs. Split declaration and assignment instead: `std::function\u003cvoid()\u003e handler; handler \u003d [\u0026] { ... handler(); };` so self-reference occurs after initialization.",
